    data: '{"model":"llama3.1:8b","messages":[{"role":"system","content":"You are a knowledgeable research assistant specializing in biomedical and scientific literature. Provide accurate, well-structured answers based on the provided context. Maintain a professional yet accessible tone, and clearly indicate when information is limited or uncertain."},{"role":"user","content":"Answer the question based on the following context from the knowledge graph.\\n\\nContext:\\nDifferential Privacy differs from cryptography-based schemes. Paths is defined as Number of paths in the module control flow graph. Recent works have focused on optimizing the performance of cryptographic tools. privacy-preserving computing schemes are based on techniques such as cryptography. Nodes is defined as Number of nodes in the module control flow graph. Privacy-preserving computation aims to introduce noncryptographic techniques to achieve privacy-preserving computing. Cryptography tools encrypt data as ciphertext. The book begins by introducing cryptographic techniques such as secret sharing, homomorphic encryption, and oblivious transfer. Privacy-preserving computing incorporates cryptography. AvePath is The average length of the paths in the module control flow graph. cryptography tools need to be used to prevent privacy leakage. cryptography tools are at the core of privacy-preserving computation. differential privacy is faster than cryptography-based schemes. traditional encrypted computation techniques are based on cryptography tools. Encrypted computation aims to introduce cryptographic techniques to achieve privacy-preserving computing. Encrypted computation uses cryptography tools. Encrypted computation guarantees cryptography-level security of data privacy. Encrypted computation is inefficient in practice due to high computational or communication complexity of the cryptography tools. TEE employs cryptography tools. Edges is defined as Number of edges in the module control flow graph. Cryptographic techniques serve as foundations of many privacy-preserving computing protocols and applications. optimizing the performance of cryptographic tools applies to machine learning. optimizing the performance of cryptographic tools applies to data mining. small-scale cases of using simple cryptography tools can be seen as early examples of privacy-preserving computing. Homomorphic Encryption is A cryptographic scheme allowing cipher computing. cryptography played an important role in military intelligence. Chapters 2-5 introduce common cryptography tools in privacy-preserving computing. schemes that employ cryptography are developed based on the difficulty of NP-hard problems. schemes that employ cryptography may be broken with increase of computational power in the future. Cycles is Total number of cycles in the module control flow graph. Multi-Party Computation uses cryptography tools. Secure Multi-Party Computing uses cryptography tools. common cryptography tools in privacy-preserving computing include secret sharing. common cryptography tools in privacy-preserving computing include homomorphic encryption. common cryptography tools in privacy-preserving computing include oblivious transfer. common cryptography tools in privacy-preserving computing include garbled circuit. Privacy Computing is Encrypted computation based on cryptography tools in a narrow sense. encrypted computation has cryptography-based security protocols at its core. simple computing tasks include averaging.  is a string\\n\\nQuestion: Graph Rag\\n\\nAnswer:"}],"temperature":0.2,"max_tokens":800}',
